From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] location and connectivity: units, permissions, unsubscribe, transport type

LocationManager:
- the portal passes the time of a fix as seconds and microseconds; the
  microseconds were added to milliseconds unconverted. 1700000000 s +
  500000 us is 1700000000500 ms now.
- providers are listed (gps, network, passive; fused from API 31), the
  last fix is kept and returned by getLastKnownLocation with its accuracy,
  time and reception time on the clock that counts during sleep;
  getCurrentLocation obeys maximum age, timeout and cancellation.
- absent altitude, speed and heading are reported as absent.
- what a listener receives follows the permission its package holds when
  the fix is delivered: fine gets the fix, coarse a position snapped to a
  grid of about 2 km at most every ten minutes, none nothing. An
  application of an API level without a permission request is asked at
  first use. A process-wide environment switch no longer decides it.
- removeUpdates works; the portal session is closed with the last
  listener, on revocation and when the process ends, and reopened with the
  accuracy the remaining listeners may have.

ConnectivityManager tells Wi-Fi, mobile data and cable apart by the
interface of the default route, reports no network as none, delivers
onLost/onAvailable/onCapabilitiesChanged on every change, and
unregisterNetworkCallback ends the subscription. NetworkCallback is a
static nested class, as applications are compiled against it.

